      "content": "The sudden failure is usually due to internal short-circuiting within the battery cells, often caused by physical damage from the swelling itself. This short circuit causes an uncontrolled, rapid release of energy, leading to thermal runaway. In thermal runaway, the heat generation exceeds the cooling rate, causing a self-accelerating chemical reaction that can result in venting or fire.",
